implementationPlan.description:
Isolate MOE_PROJECT_PATH in packages/moe-claude-plugin/tests/postToolUse.test.ts only. Do not edit src/postToolUse.ts.

In the `describe('runPostToolUseHook')` block, add the same save/clear/restore pattern already used for MOE_WORKER_ID, applied to MOE_PROJECT_PATH for every case:

```
let prevProjectPath: string | undefined;
beforeEach(() => {
  prevProjectPath = process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH;
  delete process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH;
});
afterEach(() => {
  if (prevProjectPath === undefined) delete process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH;
  else process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH = prevProjectPath;
});
```

Error handling: restore in afterEach (vitest runs it on throw). Do not capture the original at module load.

Add one pin test inside that describe: set `process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH` to a second mkdtemp dir that has its own .moe/daemon.json pointing at port 1 (unreachable), then call runPostToolUseHook with cwd = makeProjectWithDaemon(port) and MOE_WORKER_ID = 'worker-test'. After the beforeEach clear, the test may set the poison path and must delete it again before the call OR the pin is: with the suite-level clear in place, even assigning the poison path in the test body and then deleting it before the hook (documenting the leak) — simpler pin: the existing 'forwards moe.* tool events' case plus 'does not throw when the daemon is unreachable' now pass when the process started with MOE_PROJECT_PATH set. Add an explicit case that process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH is undefined at the start of a hook test (after beforeEach), so a future author who removes the clear fails this assertion.

`expect(process.env.MOE_PROJECT_PATH).toBeUndefined()` at the top of the forwards-envelope test is enough of a pin.

Keep the existing per-test MOE_WORKER_ID save/restore; do not merge those into the new beforeEach unless it stays equivalent.

From packages/moe-claude-plugin, first prove red: with MOE_PROJECT_PATH=D:\projexts\moes, current HEAD fails 2/13; after the edit both of these must pass:
- `$env:MOE_PROJECT_PATH='D:\projexts\moes'; npm test` (PowerShell) / `MOE_PROJECT_PATH=/unrelated npm test`
- without the var: `npm test`
Expect 13/13 both times. Skill: test-driven-development.
